# financial-analysis: analysis state files carry real business inputs — never commit
*.fa.json
.fa-session

# business-planning: user business data never enters this repo. bp_<slug>/
# workspaces and .bp.json state files are written into the USER's cwd; these
# entries stop them if that cwd is ever this repo, and keep the build workspace
# (real eval outputs, dogfood material) out of a `git add -A`.
bp_*/
*.bp.json
.bp-session
business-planning-workspace/

# comunicacao-executiva: N2 memory holds real audience profiles (named executives,
# their objections, internal decisions) and presentation outcomes. This repo is
# PUBLIC — that data must never enter it. Only the contract README is committed;
# the memory files themselves are written locally and stay local.
agents/comunicacao-executiva/agents/ce-memoria/audiencias/
agents/comunicacao-executiva/agents/ce-memoria/padroes-leo.md
agents/comunicacao-executiva/agents/ce-memoria/resultados.md
agents/comunicacao-executiva/agents/ce-memoria/calibracao.md

# intercom-inbox-coach: the committed workspace-config.md ships NOT_CONFIGURED.
# Baked packages carry a real roster (names, admin IDs) and inbox map — keep them out.
intercom-inbox-coach/dist/
intercom-inbox-coach/*.skill
